# Acceptance criteria

V1.7 deterministic AI hardening is complete when all of the following are true:

- [ ] `OnDeviceCoachService` no longer builds large inline free-form prompts directly inside enhancement methods.
- [ ] All on-device AI prompts are versioned through `CoachPromptPack`.
- [ ] Workout, insights, and plan copy use decision packets.
- [ ] Workout structure is always produced by deterministic code.
- [ ] Substitutions remain deterministic.
- [ ] AI output is validated before display.
- [ ] Rejected AI output falls back to deterministic copy without user-visible failure.
- [ ] Model copy cannot add unselected exercise names.
- [ ] Model copy cannot mention weights, reps, percentages, or set counts in workout summaries.
- [ ] Model copy cannot mention medical advice or raw injury details.
- [ ] Prompt version and validation outcomes are tracked without storing raw prompts or raw responses.
- [ ] `Why this workout?` uses deterministic reason codes.
- [ ] Full `swift test` passes.
- [ ] iOS simulator build succeeds.

# Risks and mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Foundation Models typed generation syntax changes across SDKs | Keep typed structs inside `#if canImport(FoundationModels)` and provide plain-string fallback. |
| Validator rejects too much good copy | Start strict for V1.7; fallback copy is acceptable. Track rejection rates. |
| Prompt pack grows too large | Keep facts compact and reason-code based. Add prompt length tests. |
| Exercise hallucination detection misses aliases | Use known exercise names first; add alias mapping later if needed. |
| Public response-model changes break call sites | Add default initializer parameters and keep metadata optional. |
| AI copy sounds too generic | Improve deterministic reason codes and templates before relaxing validator rules. |

# Recommended commit order summary

1. `chore(coach): document deterministic planner and AI copy boundary`
2. `feat(coach): add deterministic reason codes`
3. `feat(coach): derive reason codes from deterministic context`
4. `feat(coach): add structured decision packet for AI copy`
5. `feat(coach): build decision packets from deterministic responses`
6. `feat(coach): attach optional decision metadata to workout responses`
7. `feat(coach): add versioned prompt pack for on-device copy`
8. `refactor(coach): centralize deterministic copy templates`
9. `feat(coach): add isolated on-device copy editor wrapper`
10. `feat(coach): use typed Foundation Models copy responses when available`
11. `feat(coach): validate on-device coaching copy before display`
12. `feat(coach): reject AI copy that invents exercise names`
13. `feat(coach): add deterministic fallback copy helper`
14. `refactor(coach): constrain on-device workout copy with packet validation`
15. `refactor(coach): constrain on-device insights copy with validation`
16. `refactor(coach): constrain on-device plan explanation copy`
17. `test(coach): cover on-device copy accept and fallback paths`
18. `feat(coach): build workout rationale from deterministic reason codes`
19. `feat(workouts): show deterministic reason-code rationale in AI preview`
20. `feat(coach): track on-device copy validation outcomes`
21. `feat(coach): disable on-device copy after repeated validation failures`
22. `chore(coach): log safe on-device copy validation metadata`
23. `test(coach): add copy validator regression cases`
24. `test(coach): cover decision packet reason-code mapping`
25. `test(coach): verify on-device AI never changes workout structure`

# Definition of done for App Store-ready V1.7 copy hardening

The feature is App Store-ready when the app can generate workouts, insights, substitutions, and weekly-plan explanations with Foundation Models unavailable, available, and failing validation, while always preserving deterministic training decisions and never surfacing unsafe or invented copy.
